            <ArticleTitle>Morgagni hernias: an uncommon cause of chest masses in adults.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2021-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Morgagni hernia is a congenital diaphragmatic hernia that occurs secondary to potential anterior medial defects in the diaphragm. Although the hernia usually is diagnosed incidentally, appearing as a mass on chest radiograph, symptoms of bowel obstruction may occur. Surgical repair is required in all cases and may be performed with either the abdominal or transthoracic approach.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
